  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records collectively point toward temperature-dependent mechanical and tribological testing of HEAs. In particular, R1 and R18 establish HEA coatings, hardness or wear evaluation; R2-R5, R11-R14 establish strong temperature effects on deformation and dislocations; R8 supplies partial-dislocation, twinning and FCC-to-HCP mechanisms in an FCC CoNiCrFeMn HEA simulation; and R9 supplies high-temperature order-disorder modeling. Thus an expert could anticipate temperature-driven transitions from defect-mediated deformation toward disorder and softening. However, none describes the specific FeNiCrCoCu-on-Cu coating, combined nanoindentation/friction MD protocol, or the particular threshold behavior above about 900 K. Selecting that geometry and intervention would still require a substantial new idea, so the set is directionally informative but not fully reconstructive."
